---
const base = '/allagma/';
---
<div class="home-content">
  <section class="workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE RECORD IS PART OF THE RESULT</p><h2 id="workflow-title">One question. A trail you can follow.</h2></div>
    <ol class="workflow-track">
      <li><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Brief</h3><p>Define the question, materials and limits.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Plan</h3><p>Freeze the protocol and exact methods.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Attempts</h3><p>Run the work. Keep failures and recovery.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">04</span><h3>Findings</h3><p>Link claims to results and recompute them.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="first-result" aria-labelledby="first-result-title">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">START SMALL. SEE THE WHOLE PROCESS.</p><h2 id="first-result-title">Your first result,<br />on your own machine.</h2><p>The offline example compares two estimators, recovers from a failure and interruption, and writes a figure, report and claim ledger. Everything stays in ordinary files.</p><a class="text-action" href={`${base}guides/first-study/`}>Get the source and follow the tutorial <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="command-panel"><div class="command-caption">FROM YOUR SOURCE CHECKOUT</div><pre><code>python3 -m allagma toy \
  --destination work/my-first-study</code></pre><div class="command-output"><span class="check-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>24 confirmation seeds</strong><br /><span>Figure · manuscript · evidence-linked claims</span></div></div><p class="command-note">Known-answer demonstration. No LLM, GPU or paid API.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="studies-title" class="study-section">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">EXECUTED, RETAINED, INSPECTABLE</p><h2 id="studies-title">Go deeper with a real study.</h2></div><a class="text-action" href={`${base}studies/`}>Browse the evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="study-grid">
      <a class="study-card" href={`${base}studies/core-culp/`}><span class="study-number">01 / REPRODUCTION</span><h3>A graph-classification<br />capsule, reproduced.</h3><p>Six answers match the original scorer. A source labeling defect stays visible.</p><span class="study-meta">CORE CULP · Full fresh-environment replay <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      <a class="study-card" href={`${base}studies/modular-addition/`}><span class="study-number">02 / GENERALIZATION</span><h3>Better held-out accuracy.<br />No observed grokking.</h3><p>Eight training trajectories separate an endpoint improvement from a stronger claim.</p><span class="study-meta">Modular addition · Four paired seeds <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      <a class="study-card" href={`${base}studies/ema-schedule/`}><span class="study-number">03 / TRAINING DYNAMICS</span><h3>When does weight<br />averaging help?</h3><p>Duration and learning-rate policy, with paired effects and inconclusive intervals.</p><span class="study-meta">Weight EMA · 96 saved model states <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="scope-section" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">A PROCESS YOU CAN INSPECT</p><h2 id="scope-title">The agent does the work.<br />You can check the record.</h2><p>Allagma adds reusable research methods, locked campaign inputs, attempt history and evidence contracts to a coding agent. Your study owns its scientific code and statistical choices.</p><a class="text-action" href={`${base}guides/native-study/`}>Prepare a native study <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="evidence-note"><h3>What the evaluation establishes</h3><p>In twelve fresh local sessions, all twelve completed the required science. Allagma delivered <strong>6/6 complete packages</strong>; plain Codex delivered <strong>4/6</strong>.</p><p>The two gaps concern review-revision binding. This small experiment does not establish general research superiority or consistent cost savings.</p><a href={`${base}evidence/comparison/`}>Read the comparison and limitations →</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-footer-callout"><div><h2>Build a better research workflow.</h2><p>Start with a small fix, a method, or a reproducible study.</p></div><a class="primary-action" href={`${base}contributing/`}>Contribute <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  <p class="release-note">Allagma 0.3.0rc2 · Source release candidate · <a href={`${base}evidence/hosts/`}>Host boundaries</a> · <a href={`${base}project/licenses/`}>MIT core; study-specific notices</a></p>
</div>
